  "plain": "A doctor named Janini, involved in the 1996 Varginha case in Brazil, said he had never seen a bacteria like the one in that infection, before or since. The documentary filmmaker James Fox says the doctor told him this on camera. In a later episode Fox recalls it as an advanced strain that behaved as no other had, and also credits a doctor named Cesario. It matters because it points to an infection unlike anything known."
